// Terminal service — the Connect-native surface for interactive shell / PTY
// sessions on the daemon. Replaces the legacy REST surface in
// `apps/shipd/src/sessions/` (`/api/v1/sessions/...` + `/api/v1/pty-sessions`).
//
// Why a dedicated service: PTY sessions are NOT an agent concept. They are a
// dev / power-user surface, distinct from `AgentsService` (run control) and
// the canonical session projection (agent sessions). Terminal state lives in
// the L1 `ship-terminal` crate (`ship_terminal::SessionRegistry`); this
// service is the L2 Connect wire over that state.
//
// Streaming: `SessionBytes` is server-streaming (raw PTY output, byte-exact).
// `SessionEvents` is server-streaming (typed harness events, when present).
// Both use the same broadcast subscribers the legacy SSE routes used — the
// Connect adapter is the only difference.
//
// Capability policy: C0 for reads, C1 for lifecycle/IO. The `Input` blast
// is C1 because PTY input is treated as mutating the user's own space
// (matches the policy the legacy REST `/input` route enforced via
// `ManageRuns` scope).

